# class_key_no_ihash.tkr — the F4 CLASS-instantiation key-gate reject host. It proves a generic CLASS
# instantiation is constraint-checked at monomorphization (not only free generic functions): a key
# type that conforms `IEq` but not `IHash` (here `Plain`) cannot instantiate the hash-map CLASS
# `Dict<K: IEq & IHash, V>`. Before F4 this link-failed on the missing `Plain__hash`; now it is a
# clean compile-time stop. A self-contained project (its own IEq/IHash/NeByEq copies, since teko::cmp
# is compiler-internal). It has no successful build to sanitize/run (EXPECT_COMPILE_FAIL).

Feature: class_key_no_ihash — the K: IEq & IHash key gate rejects a non-IHash key at CLASS instantiation

  Scenario: class_key_without_ihash_rejected — Plain (IEq, no IHash) cannot key the hash-map class
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "does not satisfy its constraint"
